Question 16 · ASP.NET Core Web API
What is the difference between GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, and DELETE?

Frequently asked in 2-year .NET developer interviews.

First understand:
HTTP Method	Purpose
GET	Retrieve data
POST	Create new record
PUT	Update complete record
PATCH	Update partially
DELETE	Delete record

Example: Employee API
GET    /api/employee/1
POST   /api/employee
PUT    /api/employee/1
PATCH  /api/employee/1
DELETE /api/employee/1


